d whose attributes were reviewed with the other two dose reports' ahead of supporting them (D-022). The Key Object Selection Document, Mammography CAD SR, Chest CAD SR, Colon CAD SR, Procedure Log, Spectacle Prescription Report, Macular Grid Thickness and Volume Report, and Waveform Annotation SR are supported too, which adds eight more. A Key Object Selection Document is not a Structured Report by its IOD's name, but its content tree is in the same Content Sequence, built from the same content items, so it is supported, cleaned, and claimed as a report is. These eight, and the other Structured Report IODs, use no attribute that the reviewed IODs do not (D-022): their IODs add the Key Object Document, Synchronization, Enhanced General Equipment, and Timezone Modules, whose attributes the reviewed IODs already use, and none of them defines Waveform Annotation Sequence (0040,B020) or Common Instance Reference. The others are sequestered, as above, until each is supported. Rendition Selection Document is among PS3.3's Structured Report IODs but has no Storage SOP Class in the pinned Table B.5-1, so no instance is classified as one, and a SOP Class UID that names it would be sequestered as not a Standard Storage SOP Class. A Procedure Log orders its entries by increasing Observation DateTime (0040,A032) (PS3.3 Section A.35.7.3.1.2), which D would give one constant, so under a policy that neither keeps nor modifies that datetime each entry takes the dummy datetime of its rank (D-021), and a log whose entries are not in that order is sequestered (D-047). On 31 October 2026 the maintainer brought the 22 other RT IODs of Table B.5-1 into the first supported release, in this order: RT Ion Plan and RT Ion Beams Treatment Record; RT Brachy Treatment Record and RT Treatment Summary Record; Enhanced RT Image and Enhanced Continuous RT Image; and the 16 second-generation RT IODs, RT Physician Intent, RT Segment Annotation, RT Radiation Set, RT Radiation Record Set, RT Radiation Salvage Record, RT Treatment Preparation, RT Patient Position Acquisition Instruction, RT Beams Delivery Instruction, RT Brachy Application Setup Delivery Instruction, RT Radiation Set Delivery Instruction, and the C-Arm Photon-Electron, Tomotherapeutic, and Robotic-Arm Radiation IODs and their Records. As for the IODs added on 25 October, each one's text, UID, and date attributes are reviewed ahead of supporting it (D-022), and each is supported in a change of its own, which settles where its plain X and its D sequester an instance (D-020, D-021); until then each is sequestered. RT Ion Plan and RT Ion Beams Treatment Record are supported, which adds two IODs. An RT Ion Plan describes a treatment with beams of protons or heavier ions, and an RT Ion Beams Treatment Record what was delivered of one; neither holds pixel data, so neither can show a face or hold burned-in text. An RT Ion Plan names its structure set, its RT Doses, and the plans related to it, in Referenced Structure Set Sequence (300C,0060), Referenced Dose Sequence (300C,0080), and Referenced RT Plan Sequence (300C,0002), and an RT Ion Beams Treatment Record names the plan that it records in Referenced RT Plan Sequence, by UIDs that the run's key replaces as it replaces the referenced instances' own (D-003), so a written record still names the written plan. Their text that Table E.1-1 omits has rules reviewed ahead of supporting them (D-022), and they add no place where the Basic Profile's actions sequester an instance beyond those that RT Plan and RT Beams Treatment Record have: Responsible Person and Responsible Organization in the Patient Module (D-020). The Institution Code Sequence of the person who resolved an interlock, here in Treatment Session Ion Beam Sequence (3008,0021), takes the reviewed dummy item that it takes in an RT Beams Treatment Record (D-021). RT Brachy Treatment Record and RT Treatment Summary Record are supported, which adds two IODs. An RT Brachy Treatment Record says what an af